Thanks [user]. For reference, the SBOM and Scan actions wrap the Syft and Grype commands. To run these directly, perform a standard NiFi package or install build with Maven, and then run these two commands:


{noformat}
syft scan file:nifi-assembly/target/nifi-2.2.0-SNAPSHOT-bin.zip --output syft-json=/tmp/nifi-assembly.json
grype sbom:/tmp/nifi-assembly.json
{noformat}

Although it is possible to run Grype directly, using Syft to produce the intermediate SBOM is useful for cataloging dependencies.

